<servinfosub id = "AENLSB0A1621004002">
<title>
Thermostat Heater Operation
</title>
<ptxt>
When electric current is applied to heater (1) controlled by ECM, wax (2) is heated and expands and then squeeze out valve to open. On the other hand, this thermostat also responds to coolant temperature without electric current as the conventional type does and starts open at 97 &#176;C (206.6 &#176;F) and fully opens at 110 &#176;C (230 &#176;F). Refer to 
<intxref refid = "AENLSB0A1626008">Thermostat Heater Inspection:K14D</intxref>
.
</ptxt>
